            <div xml:id="d36">

                <pb facs="0135" n="31" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg31"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3542: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-17T11:00:00+08:00">January 17, 1932—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 17—3:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>82. Following from American Consul General at Mukden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“January 16, 1 p.m. Telegram No. 32. Headquarters reports that a Japanese
                            battalion occupied Tungliao January 14, noon, after ejecting 3,000
                            Chinese partisans; losses, Chinese 60, Japanese 0.</p>
                        <p>Reliable information is to the effect that these so-called partisans
                            belonged to the Third Cavalry Brigade of which about 1,000 were in
                            Tungliao.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
